{
  "duration": 83.68,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.259,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.919,
      "end": 1.839,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.44,
      "end": 3.559,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.0,
      "end": 5.5,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.92,
      "end": 8.179,
      "text": "a train crosses a two-kilometer-long tunnel"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.679,
      "end": 10.219,
      "text": "in three minutes, 20 seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.739,
      "end": 11.42,
      "text": "The question is"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.979,
      "end": 15.239,
      "text": "asking us to find the speed of the train in kilometer"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.719,
      "end": 16.219,
      "text": "per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.76,
      "end": 18.939,
      "text": "So the total distance covered is two kilometer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.479,
      "end": 22.879,
      "text": "but the time is given in minutes and seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.639,
      "end": 25.84,
      "text": "Since the speed is asked in kilometer per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.319,
      "end": 28.879,
      "text": "we first need to convert the time into hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.559,
      "end": 31.319,
      "text": "Three minutes, 20 seconds means"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.819,
      "end": 34.0,
      "text": "three minutes is equal to three into"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.36,
      "end": 34.5,
      "text": "60,"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.099,
      "end": 36.679,
      "text": "which is 180 seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.18,
      "end": 38.979,
      "text": "Adding the remaining 20 seconds, we get"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.659,
      "end": 40.479,
      "text": "180 plus"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.779,
      "end": 40.939,
      "text": "20,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.379,
      "end": 42.599,
      "text": "which is 200 seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.939,
      "end": 46.159,
      "text": "Now we know that one hour is equal to"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.5,
      "end": 48.279,
      "text": "3,600 seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.68,
      "end": 51.539,
      "text": "So to convert seconds into hours, we divide by"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.939,
      "end": 56.879,
      "text": "3,600. Therefore, 200 seconds is equal to 200 divided by"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.299,
      "end": 58.859,
      "text": "3,600 hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.359,
      "end": 60.539,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.959,
      "end": 62.559,
      "text": "we get one by 18 hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.039,
      "end": 64.099,
      "text": "Now we know the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.519,
      "end": 67.0,
      "text": "Speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.419,
      "end": 71.939,
      "text": "Putting the values, speed is equal to two divided by one by 18."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.559,
      "end": 73.699,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.159,
      "end": 78.719,
      "text": "we get 36 kilometer per hour. So the speed of the train is"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.279,
      "end": 80.719,
      "text": "36 kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.299,
      "end": 83.68,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option C."
    }
